# Territory Painting

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M1 Technical proofs
Dependencies: `02_DOMAIN_RULES.todo`, `03_PLAYER_CAMERA_INPUT.todo`

## Purpose

Prove deterministic, performant floor territory whose logical ownership matches its visual representation.

## Tasks

- [ ] Implement paintable-surface registration.
- [ ] Implement world-to-territory coordinate mapping.
- [ ] Implement logical field storage.
- [ ] Implement spray stamp commands.
- [ ] Implement reset.
- [ ] Implement coverage queries.
- [ ] Implement territory sampling beneath a player.
- [ ] Implement visual mask stamping.
- [ ] Implement ownership debug overlay.
- [ ] Implement sustained-spray benchmark.
- [ ] Compare candidate CPU/GPU split approaches.
- [ ] Record territory authority decision.
- [ ] Add deterministic sequence tests.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Visual and logical ownership align for all test stamps.
- [ ] Score is deterministic.
- [ ] Full reset leaves no stale logical or visual paint.
- [ ] Sustained spray meets provisional CPU/GPU budgets.
- [ ] Memory usage is bounded and documented.
- [ ] Territory can be sampled without GPU readback.

